{"layout_dets": [{"category_type": "text_block", "poly": [264.9759, 315.9989, 1370.9982, 315.9989, 1370.9982, 392.952, 264.9759, 392.952], "ignore": false, "order": 2, "anno_id": "box_id_0", "attribute": {}, "text": "Hence $ {a}_{1} $ is the slope of the secant line passing through the two points $ \\left( {{x}_{0},f\\left( {x}_{0}\\right) }\\right) $ and $ \\left( {{x}_{1},f\\left( {x}_{1}\\right) }\\right) $ ."}, {"category_type": "text_block", "poly": [263.9841, 392.952, 1370.9982, 392.952, 1370.9982, 468.96950000000004, 263.9841, 468.96950000000004], "ignore": false, "order": 3, "anno_id": "box_id_1", "attribute": {}, "text": "The coefficients $ {a}_{0} $ and $ {a}_{1} $ are the same for both $ {P}_{1}\\left( x\\right) $ and $ {P}_{2}\\left( x\\right) $. Evaluating (2) at the node $ {x}_{2} $ , we find that"}, {"category_type": "equation_isolated", "poly": [266.29901123046875, 494.9324, 1218.9222000000002, 494.9324, 1218.9222000000002, 537.97, 266.29901123046875, 537.97], "ignore": false, "order": 4, "anno_id": "box_id_2", "attribute": {}, "latex": "$$f\\left( {x}_{2}\\right)  = {P}_{2}\\left( {x}_{2}\\right)  = {a}_{0} + {a}_{1}\\left( {{x}_{2}\\;{x}_{0}}\\right)  + {a}_{2}\\left( {{x}_{2}\\;{x}_{0}}\\right) \\left( {{x}_{2}\\;{x}_{1}}\\right) .\\tag{11}$$"}, {"category_type": "text_block", "poly": [263.9841, 560.8922, 1152.9675, 560.8922, 1152.9675, 602.0586000000001, 263.9841, 602.0586000000001], "ignore": false, "order": 5, "anno_id": "box_id_3", "attribute": {}, "text": "The values for $ {a}_{0} $ and $ {a}_{1} $ in (9) and (10) can be used in (11) to obtain"}, {"category_type": "equation_isolated", "poly": [452.922, 617.9638, 885.0932322704566, 617.9638, 885.0932322704566, 705.6833894722174, 452.922, 705.6833894722174], "ignore": false, "order": 6, "anno_id": "box_id_4", "attribute": {}, "latex": "$$a_2 = \\frac{ f(x_2) \\quad a_0 \\quad a_1(x_2 \\quad x_0 )}{(x_2 \\quad x_0)(x_2 \\quad x_1)}$$"}, {"category_type": "text_block", "poly": [267.9513, 813.0364000000001, 1120.0728, 813.0364000000001, 1120.0728, 852.0977, 267.9513, 852.0977], "ignore": false, "order": 8, "anno_id": "box_id_5", "attribute": {}, "text": "For computational purposes we prefer to write this last quantity as"}, {"category_type": "equation_isolated", "poly": [268.1627502441406, 870.108, 1184.0439000000001, 870.108, 1184.0439000000001, 962.0307, 268.1627502441406, 962.0307], "ignore": false, "order": 9, "anno_id": "box_id_6", "attribute": {}, "latex": "$$a_2 = \\left( \\frac{f(x_2)f(x_1)}{{x_2}~{x_1}} \\quad \\quad \\frac{f(x_1)f(x_0)}{{x_1}~{x_0}} \\quad \\right) / (x_2 \\quad x_0).\\tag{12}$$"}, {"category_type": "text_block", "poly": [266.9595, 979.1054, 1376.9489999999998, 979.1054, 1376.9489999999998, 1133.0116, 266.9595, 1133.0116], "ignore": false, "order": 10, "anno_id": "box_id_7", "attribute": {}, "text": "The two formulas for $ {a}_{2} $ can be shown to be equivalent by writing the quotients over the common denominator $( {x}_{2} \\quad {x}_{1}) ( {x}_{2} \\quad {x}_{0}) ({x}_{1} \\quad {x}_{0} )$ . The details are left for the reader. The numerator in (12) is the difference between the first-order divided differences. In order to proceed, we need to introduce the idea of divided differences."}, {"category_type": "text_block", "poly": [268.9431, 1163.8863999999999, 1373.9736, 1163.8863999999999, 1373.9736, 1241.0734, 268.9431, 1241.0734], "ignore": false, "order": 11, "anno_id": "box_id_8", "attribute": {}, "text": "Definition 4.1 (Divided Differences). The divided differences for a function $ f\\left( x\\right) $ are defined as follows:"}, {"category_type": "equation_isolated", "poly": [629.3274626308807, 1256.9786, 846.656136947287, 1256.9786, 846.656136947287, 1302.7578125, 629.3274626308807, 1302.7578125], "ignore": false, "order": 12, "anno_id": "box_id_9", "attribute": {}, "latex": "$$f[x_k] = f(x_k),$$"}, {"category_type": "text_block", "poly": [265.9677, 1580.9300999999998, 1169.0016, 1580.9300999999998, 1169.0016, 1623.0321, 265.9677, 1623.0321], "ignore": false, "order": 16, "anno_id": "box_id_10", "attribute": {}, "text": "The recursive rule for constructing higher-order divided differences is"}, {"category_type": "equation_isolated", "poly": [268.1627502441406, 1638.9373, 1302.0681, 1638.9373, 1302.0681, 1733.9007, 268.1627502441406, 1733.9007], "ignore": false, "order": 17, "anno_id": "box_id_11", "attribute": {}, "latex": "$$f\\left\\lbrack  {{x}_{k\\;j},{x}_{k\\;j + 1},\\ldots ,{x}_{k}}\\right\\rbrack   = \\frac{f\\left\\lbrack  {{x}_{k\\;j + 1},\\ldots ,{x}_{k}}\\right\\rbrack \\quad f\\left\\lbrack  {{x}_{k\\;j},\\ldots ,{x}_{k\\;1}}\\right\\rbrack  }{{x}_{k}\\quad{x}_{k\\;j}}\\tag{14}$$"}, {"category_type": "text_block", "poly": [271.9185, 1749.1042, 1043.0430000000001, 1749.1042, 1043.0430000000001, 1790.0366999999999, 271.9185, 1790.0366999999999], "ignore": false, "order": 18, "anno_id": "box_id_12", "attribute": {}, "text": "and is used to construct the divided differences in Table 4.8."}, {"category_type": "text_block", "poly": [270.9267, 1808.047, 1379.9243999999999, 1808.047, 1379.9243999999999, 1885.0001, 270.9267, 1885.0001], "ignore": false, "order": 20, "anno_id": "box_id_13", "attribute": {}, "text": "The coefficients $ {a}_{k} $ of $ {P}_{N}\\left( x\\right) $ depend on the values $ f\\left( {x}_{j}\\right) $, for $ j = 0,1,\\ldots ,k $. The next theorem shows that ${a}_{k}$ can be computed using divided differences:"}, {"category_type": "equation_isolated", "poly": [271.8902587890625, 1910.963, 982.0473, 1910.963, 982.0473, 1953.0649999999998, 271.8902587890625, 1953.0649999999998], "ignore": false, "order": 21, "anno_id": "box_id_14", "attribute": {}, "latex": "$${a}_{k} = f\\left\\lbrack  {{x}_{0},{x}_{1},\\ldots ,{x}_{k}}\\right\\rbrack  .\\tag{15}$$"}, {"category_type": "header", "poly": [264.9759, 239.98139999999998, 707.9799, 239.98139999999998, 707.9799, 275.0664, 264.9759, 275.0664], "ignore": false, "order": 0, "anno_id": "box_id_15", "attribute": {}, "text": "Sec. 4.4 NEWTON POLYNOMIALS"}, {"category_type": "page_number", "poly": [1318.9287000000002, 239.98139999999998, 1369.0146, 239.98139999999998, 1369.0146, 271.0901, 1318.9287000000002, 271.0901], "ignore": false, "order": 1, "anno_id": "box_id_16", "attribute": {}, "text": "223"}, {"category_type": "abandon", "poly": [1350.0050999999999, 1760.0974999999999, 1374.9654, 1760.0974999999999, 1374.9654, 1787.9316, 1350.0050999999999, 1787.9316], "ignore": false, "order": 19, "anno_id": "box_id_17", "attribute": {}, "text": ""}, {"category_type": "equation_isolated", "poly": [493.6759033203125, 710.0868530273438, 1182.5288488662288, 710.0868530273438, 1182.5288488662288, 801.4103393554688, 493.6759033203125, 801.4103393554688], "ignore": false, "order": 7, "anno_id": "box-ur8e9szp", "attribute": {}, "latex": "$$= \\left( \\frac{f(x_2)~f(x_0)}{{x_2}~{x_0}} \\qquad \\frac{f(x_1)~f(x_0)}{{x_1}~{x_0}} \\quad \\right) / (x_2 \\quad x_1).$$"}, {"category_type": "equation_isolated", "poly": [555.1795043945312, 1308.3489990234375, 1000.6145629882812, 1308.3489990234375, 1000.6145629882812, 1394.081298828125, 555.1795043945312, 1394.081298828125], "ignore": false, "order": 13, "anno_id": "box-3j91jxd6", "attribute": {}, "latex": "$$f[x_{k~~1}, x_k] = \\frac{f[x_k]~f[x_{k~~1}]}{{x_k}~ x_{k~1}},$$"}, {"category_type": "equation_isolated", "poly": [270.0265197753906, 1394.081298828125, 1155.305419921875, 1394.081298828125, 1155.305419921875, 1479.8135986328125, 270.0265197753906, 1479.8135986328125], "ignore": false, "order": 14, "anno_id": "box-3dv2w0e1", "attribute": {}, "latex": "$$f[x_{k\\quad2}, x_{k\\quad1}, x_k] = \\frac{f[x_{k\\quad1},x_k]\\quad f[x_{k\\quad2}, x_{k\\quad1}]}{x_k\\quad x_{k\\quad2}} ,\\tag{13}$$"}, {"category_type": "equation_isolated", "poly": [404.2161560058594, 1483.541015625, 1308.1324462890625, 1483.541015625, 1308.1324462890625, 1567.4095458984375, 404.2161560058594, 1567.4095458984375], "ignore": false, "order": 15, "anno_id": "box-z10z1vt4", "attribute": {}, "latex": "$$f[x_{k\\quad 3}, x_{k\\quad 2}, x_{k\\quad 1}, x_k] = \\frac{f[x_{k\\quad 2}, x_{k\\quad 1}, x_k]\\quad f[x_{k\\quad 3}, x_{k\\quad 2}, x_{k\\quad 1}]}{x_k\\quad  x_{k\\quad 3}} .$$"}, {"category_type": "equation_semantic", "poly": [450.5853785182178, 612.5416240590255, 1191.0004175807173, 612.5416240590255, 1191.0004175807173, 807.387704492264, 450.5853785182178, 807.387704492264], "ignore": false, "order": null, "anno_id": "box-3djlejnf", "attribute": {}, "text": ""}, {"category_type": "equation_semantic", "poly": [270.9881273197093, 1252.9921744851615, 1311.296715521058, 1252.9921744851615, 1311.296715521058, 1573.2174496982295, 270.9881273197093, 1573.2174496982295], "ignore": false, "order": null, "anno_id": "box-c567ixf2", "attribute": {}, "text": ""}], "page_info": {"page_no": 0, "height": 2339, "width": 1653, "image_path": "page-0a262e27-b24d-4429-9b21-90563d4fada7.png", "page_attribute": {"data_source": "book", "language": "english", "layout": "single_column", "special_issue": [], "subset": "equation_hard"}}, "extra": {"relation": []}, "_eval_tags": {"is_clean": true, "has_watermark": false, "has_fuzzy_scan": false, "has_colorful_bg": false, "layout": "single_column"}}